              "id": "plan-the-first-purchase-and-decide-what-comes-after",
              "kind": "ask",
              "config": {
                "name": "ai",
                "input": {
                  "do": "In the same answer, name the service and the result the customer wants. Draft one concrete first purchase: its result, what is included, exactly when it ends, and its one-time price. Then ask what useful work still remains once that first result is delivered. If evidence supports continuing work, draft it separately with its scope, price, billing interval and how to stop, all in the same currency. It starts only after a separate explicit opt-in. Buying the first result must never start recurring billing. If no recurring need is observed or evidence is insufficient, stop at the first purchase and omit all ongoing terms. Plan one small later test of whether people understand what each purchase costs and when it ends. State what to measure and what would stop the test; compare like-for-like costs if comparing prices. Return a planning draft only. Do not send, publish, charge, enroll, or say the test ran.",
                  "submit": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "oneOf": [
                      {
                        "type": "object",
                        "properties": {
                          "choice": {
                            "const": "offer-ongoing-support"
                          },
                          "service": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "minLength": 1,
                            "pattern": "\\S"
                          },
                          "customer_outcome": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "minLength": 1,
                            "pattern": "\\S"
                          },
                          "currency": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "pattern": "^[A-Z]{3}$"
                          },
